    purpose: "A microcontroller's own ADC is usually 10 or 12 bits and often noisy or non-linear. External ADCs measure small or precise signals properly: load cells (weighing scales), thermocouples, RTDs, strain gauges, batteries and sensor bridges. The ADS1115 is a friendly 16-bit, 4-channel converter on I²C with a programmable gain amplifier (PGA), up to 860 samples per second. The ADS1220 is a 24-bit converter on SPI with a gain of up to 128, built-in excitation current sources and an internal reference, designed for bridges and temperature sensors. The ADS1256 is a 24-bit, 8-channel, up to 30,000 samples per second converter for high-resolution data acquisition.",
