    purpose: "Lithium cells must be charged carefully: too much voltage or current causes swelling, damage or fire. The TP4056 (up to 1 A, 8-pin package) and TP4054 (up to 500 mA, 5-pin SOT-23) do it properly for one 3.7 V nominal cell, ending at 4.2 V ±1 %. They are the heart of the ubiquitous blue USB charging boards and of countless rechargeable gadgets, so you can add USB charging to a project with one chip, two or three resistors and a couple of capacitors. They charge only; protecting the cell against over-discharge, short circuits and overcharge faults is a separate job, usually done by a protection IC on the cell or module.",
